     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Port auxiliary infrastructure (fenders) rehabilitated 
Indicator: Port fendering system rehabilitated to be resilient to climate change and disaster impacts 
Progress/Status: Contract for the rehabilitation of the fenders was signed on 6 March 2023 for AU$1.09 million (US$0.71 million equivalent) The contract price has been increased to AU$1.36 million ($0.89 million equivalent) through four variations in 2024. Disbursement has reached AU$1.35 million ($0.88 million). Nine super cone fenders have been installed at the international berth and eight arch fenders at the domestic berth. The original 8 arch fenders were installed by 30 November 2023 and the original nine super cone fenders were installed by 31 March 2024, with the last fender being installed on 3 December 2024.

To date, two instances of damage due to improper mooring have been reported. An ADB mission in April 2025 has recommended the IA to appoint a supervisor responsible for proper use of the port including: (i) designation of wharf to berth, (ii) periodic check on fender status and mooring, and (iii) claiming of compensation for damage, when required. The defect liability period ends in January 2026. 
Data Source: Project design and quarterly project progress report 
